# rt_ipc_rust: Rust reimplementation of the migrating-thread real-time IPC.
#

config RT_IPC_RUST
	tristate "Real-time IPC (migrating-thread model), Rust reimplementation"
	depends on RUST
	depends on MMU
	help
	  rt_ipc_rust is a Rust counterpart to the C RT_IPC subsystem.  It
	  reproduces the same object model -- reference-counted endpoints
	  registered by servers, client connections bound to an endpoint and a
	  synchronous migrating-thread call path -- using the kernel's Rust
	  abstractions, and exposes it through the /dev/rt_ipc_rust control
	  device.

	  Objects are identified by integer handles managed in a global table
	  rather than by anonymous-inode file descriptors, because the Rust VFS
	  layer does not yet provide anon-inode / SCM_RIGHTS fd passing.  As in
	  the C foundation, the low-level partial context switch into the server
	  is not yet wired up, so RT_IPC_RUST_CALL performs the full setup and
	  then returns -EOPNOTSUPP.

	  To compile this as a module, choose M here: the module will be called
	  rt_ipc_rust.

	  If unsure, say N.
